  "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Find $3a+2b.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply each component of $a$ by $3$ and each component of $b$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2b & =3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9-6 \\\\ 6-4 \\\\ 15+2 \\\\ 3+10 \\\\ -6+12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 17 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
